WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.720
Aksel?
- Your hubby is back from a night club!

2
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.120
What is going on?

3
00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:13.760
Your hubby was... yeah...
Estonian man is a thancing wachine.

4
00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.600
Dear God, are you hurt?

5
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:23.760
No. You should see the other guys.
Some brats attacked me.

6
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.400
A bunch of brats...

7
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:29.840
Jesus! Dear God!
What are you doing?

8
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.160
Put that down and help me.

9
00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.600
Hell!
- My head hurts...

10
00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:41.560
Sure it does if you come home
an axe lodged in your skull.

11
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.120
Dear God! He’s going to throw up.
Bring me a bowl.

12
00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.360
He cannot hold his liquor.

13
00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.240
I was a hit!
- I can see that.

14
00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:53.320
I was really popular!
- Wait, wait.

15
00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:56.280
Come here!
- Don’t... Listen...

16
00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.960
You should have seen how
all the women went crazy!

17
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.760
Right.
- Come here.

18
00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:03.880
Aksel, stop it.

19
00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:09.640
All the men envied... envied me.

20
00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.920
Are you joking?
He will miss it.

21
00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.520
Dear God!

22
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:26.000
Dance, dance, dance. Come here.

23
00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:29.960
Oh, it’s you Mihkel.

24
00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:34.440
Handsome boy. My son.

25
00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:41.280
Shoot, shoot, shoot.
Your dad is bleeding.

26
00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.560
DIVORCE IN PEACE

27
00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.240
It’s not just the domestic staff,
whining about scrubbing the floors.

28
00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:55.600
I love everything in its proper place.

29
00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.840
But it gets on my nerves
that Laura doesn’t respect my efforts.

30
00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:05.040
I’m saying that men implicitly assume
that household is on wife’s shoulders.

31
00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:10.760
Then they beat one’s chest
after picking up their underwear once

32
00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.760
and throwing it into dirty laundry box.

33
00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:16.360
I’m telling, damn it, on the contrary.
I have to pick up your panties.

34
00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:19.440
What’s wrong with picking up
my panties, when I have to work.

35
00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:23.480
Yes? No.

36
00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:26.880
We had tacit agreement,
when we moved in together.

37
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:32.320
We’ll respect the others interests,
hobbies, passions. Wasn’t it so?

38
00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:33.600
Well?

39
00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:37.160
Her only interest is
to make money 24/7.

40
00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:41.320
What can I do, when she does
nothing else but makes money?

41
00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:44.520
Did she study to be a jeweller
so she could sell buns?

42
00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:49.800
First, earning money is not my passion,
what it would be used for is important.

43
00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:53.600
There’s no difference.
- There’s no difference?

44
00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:56.560
I wanted to create for us a beautiful
and cosy home.

45
00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:58.840
And you did. Congratulations!
- And I did.

46
00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:04.080
Then out of a blue an idea, a project,
where our home had no place.

47
00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.680
I opened my eyes one morning
and there was absolutely nothing.

48
00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.680
My eyes were open all the time.

49
00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:13.200
What? You just fiddle with your violin
and whine all the time.

50
00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.640
OK. You wash the floors now and then.

51
00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:18.440
You just love to see things
the way you like to see them.

52
00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:19.960
Very good.

53
00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:24.160
Let’s move on
to our next therapy mission.

54
00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:28.640
It’s “The Altar of Wishes”.

55
00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:36.240
Magic potion. Fixes everything.
- What is this?

56
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:40.560
The world’s best hangover remedy.
My personal secret formula.

57
00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:47.000
It’s gross!
- Gross? It fixes all at one stroke.

58
00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:53.160
I’ll really need that kind of medicine,
which would fix everything at once.

59
00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:57.720
It’ll fix physical. We’ll focus
on your mental health later.

60
00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.720
It tastes like badger’s piss.

61
00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:11.920
What? It’s really badger’s piss?
Bloody hunters’ Alka-Seltzer!

62
00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:16.760
Its’ cucumber water
and some other components.

63
00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:21.760
Perfectly neat stuff. Drink it up!
Piss!

64
00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:27.120
A few bruises wouldn’t hurt a man.

65
00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:30.120
Actually this blow hit the right spot.

66
00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:35.920
A wake-up call. I feel good,
kind of masculine feeling.

67
00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:43.640
Sure, a masculine feeling. Drink it!
Very good. It’ll go right down.

68
00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:50.520
You and Ülo should look for a rental.

69
00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:54.280
We all have to move out soon.
I can help you if you need.

70
00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:57.280
We’ll go away to Spain soon
to join a protest action.

71
00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:06.480
This Ülo is also a kind of protest?
It can’t be that you and Ülo…

72
00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:10.080
You can’t understand.
You simply can’t understand.

73
00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.200
You are too small a person
to understand these things.

74
00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:17.200
But let’s talk. Let’s speak honestly,
what is troubling you

75
00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:21.120
and this person can return...
- What’s the matter? Really?

76
00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:23.560
Why else… Sorry, but…

77
00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:28.000
I’m worried about animals, birds,

78
00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:31.720
because I have no strength to worry
about you and dad anymore.

79
00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:35.320
You couldn’t care less.
- Ave!

80
00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.200
At least dad has been at home.

81
00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:40.520
I couldn’t talk to him,
but at least he has been here.

82
00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:42.600
You have never been around.

83
00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:51.640
I have to go to the training assembly,
but Mirjam is all over me.

84
00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:56.840
Is everything all right?
- We had this complete honesty evening.

85
00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:01.560
After that you can swallow poison
and die.

86
00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:06.920
Do you know what shocked me most?

87
00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:19.120
Mirjam said she’s not a hunting trophy.
Do I take her for a hunting trophy?

88
00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:20.920
I worship her!

89
00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:25.240
She told your divorce
has made her think.

90
00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:27.800
Sorry, sorry.

91
00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:31.120
I can’t imagine what would happen
if I’ll find her with another man.

92
00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:35.240
I would pick up a machine gun,
I would take a tank…

93
00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:40.840
You are a nice and calm man.

94
00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:44.520
Can stand by and watch patiently,
when your wife with this Rihard…

95
00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:48.400
But I really don’t know,
what I would do.

96
00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:55.360
So the fifth therapy mission –
“The Altar of Wishes”.

97
00:06:56.920 --> 00:07:00.920
You’ll built using domestic tools
a small lovely altar,

98
00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:05.400
write down on paper your wishes
to your partner for his new life.

99
00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:08.240
You lay these papers on the altar.

100
00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:13.440
Use candles, spiritual music.

101
00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:17.840
Built together for your ending marriage
a small lovely shrine.

102
00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:22.360
Very… spiritual.

103
00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:40.320
I see! Things have come to this -
you’ll bring a date into our kitchen!

104
00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:44.800
Aksel, stop it. It’s…
I’m having a business meeting.

105
00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:46.760
Are you taking me for a complete fool?

106
00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:50.360
You say that I’m this and that,
you don’t like anything about me!

107
00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:53.920
But you have chosen a replacement
long time ago! – Stop! It’s business.

108
00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:57.400
Business? It’s all business for you!

109
00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:00.160
Jumping in and out of a bed
is business to her!

110
00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:03.560
Excuse me, I was going to…
- You are going nowhere! Let’s talk!

111
00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:06.440
Excuse me, Rihard.
Aksel, come on. Be sensible.

112
00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:09.640
You consider yourself a tough guy,
who can buy everything you fancy.

113
00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:13.720
If you want my wife, then come
and fight with me, bloody hell!

114
00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:17.600
My God, Aksel! Please.
- Are you a man or not? Come!

115
00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:21.320
Are you stupid or what?

116
00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:24.600
Who is stupid right now?
Who is stupid?

117
00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:32.160
I have no relationship with Rihard
but a business relationship.

118
00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:36.160
I’m selling him my cake shop,
our bakery,

119
00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:38.600
because you want a half of it.

120
00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:41.920
Rihard wants to expand
his restaurant business to the bakery.

121
00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:46.840
Well, this all looked like…
- Extremely embarrassing, extremely.

122
00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:50.480
I think I have to talk to Rihard.

123
00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:53.600
Of course! Right,
you have to talk to “him”.

124
00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:58.120
There’s no need to talk to me. Right?
Go, go and save your business.

125
00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:03.200
Let’s speak then. Please explain to me,
what this was all about?

126
00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:11.160
You could understand
that I got it all wrong.

127
00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:19.560
From my point of view
this all looks suspicious, patronizing.

128
00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:24.640
I’m just a small worm,
nobody cares to explain anything.

129
00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:31.200
This has gone wrong
from the beginning.

130
00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:34.480
Slanted, right?
- Yes, it has been slanted.

131
00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:39.440
Let’s everybody accuse me!
It’s all my fault!

132
00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:43.600
I have been working my ass off
to keep this all running.

133
00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:48.880
I’m pleased that… If it’s true
that you don’t have a thing for Rihard…

134
00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.600
Now you are pleased?

135
00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:55.600
All right.
Please start building the altar.

136
00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:59.000
I’ll go and see
is there anything to be saved.

137
00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:04.680
We were supposed
to build the altar together.

138
00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:24.920
Aksel.
- Mirjam?

139
00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:28.120
I can see you are more masculine.
- What do you mean?

140
00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:32.040
Well, scars become you
my violin hero, bow master.

141
00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:36.440
Listen, Mirjam, we can’t talk.
It’s dangerous, you know. Tauno, he…

142
00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:38.560
Suit yourself!

143
00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:59.480
Now we have to write down our wishes.

144
00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:07.320
I wish you well.
- Me too.

145
00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:13.960
Let’s write it down.

146
00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:19.280
Right. Let’s write.
- Would we read out our wishes?

147
00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:24.240
If you’ll show me yours,
I’ll show you mine.

148
00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:27.680
OK. It’s a deal.

149
00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:34.840
“Dear Aksel, remember me…”

150
00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:38.440
“Laura, I wish you…”

151
00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:42.240
“I wish you on your journey…”

152
00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:46.840
“Be always good and smart!”

153
00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:21.720
It’s really pretty, Aksel.
- I sincerely wish you all the best.

154
00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:25.120
Thank you!
- You’re welcome!

155
00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:37.440
Let it be a constant reminder
of all the beautiful we are giving up.

156
00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:42.200
Bloody hell!
- Jesus!

157
00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:50.040
Come back! Don’t do that!
- Don’t you… Let it burn.

158
00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:04.320
I wasn’t away from home all the time.

159
00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:10.080
Well, you were quite a lot.
- What do you mean?

160
00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:14.480
We and dad even joked about it.

161
00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:16.880
You and dad?
- Yes, we and dad.

162
00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:20.640
Dad used to take us sledging,
when we were brats.

163
00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:23.920
This joke originates from there.

164
00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:28.800
I’m not sure I want to hear this.
- It’s was nothing awful.

165
00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:31.680
No, let it be.
- OK.

166
00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:40.200
Well, tell then.
- Do you want to hear?

167
00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:44.760
Dad used to say that mom is as rare
as a five leaf lilac blossom.

168
00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:56.200
Strange. That’s not how I remember.

169
00:13:56.320 --> 00:13:58.800
I remember being with you and…

170
00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:02.280
People remember exceptional things
more intensely than routine ones.

171
00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:04.920
Dad was a routine, you a holiday.

172
00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:11.320
Actually it’s okay.

173
00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:14.360
We both understood
that making herbarium

174
00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:18.320
and listening to music with dad
would hardly put bread on the table.

175
00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:22.640
Don’t worry!

176
00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:40.360
What’s now?

177
00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:46.920
I thought that now,
when we are officially at war,

178
00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:51.400
you should look under your car
before starting it in the morning

179
00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:55.560
to check that brake hose is intact.

180
00:14:55.680 --> 00:14:59.520
Yes, and you should let the cat
to have a bite.

181
00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:04.200
Why? Why the cat?
- Maybe I have poisoned your food.

182
00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:10.400
Right. That was good one.

183
00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:14.320
The cat. Watch out!

184
00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:20.080
Aksel.
- Yes?

185
00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:26.600
We’ll see each other
from a new perspective.

186
00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:33.680
You see yourself through my eyes
and I myself through yours.

187
00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:37.160
I have now a better understanding
of some things.

188
00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:47.360
Aksel.

189
00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:50.800
Yes?

190
00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:54.920
Good night!

191
00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:01.040
Good night!

192
00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:04.200
Aksel!
- Yes?

193
00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:11.200
Are you going to be all right,
when we all go our separate ways?

194
00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:14.760
You have your students
and music school.

195
00:16:14.880 --> 00:16:16.440
I will.

196
00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:22.920
I will be okay. Don’t worry.

197
00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:28.480
Good night!
- Good night!

198
00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:43.600
You didn’t say “Aksel” anymore?
- No.

199
00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:52.120
I will close the door then.
- Yes.

200
00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:06.480
Wait, wait! Why are you intruding
into my house? Into my home?

201
00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:08.400
Excuse me, who you are?
- Hello.

202
00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:10.800
Hello. Who are you?
- I’m Roberta’s father.

203
00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:13.360
Roberta’s father? Excuse me.
What Roberta’s father?

204
00:17:13.480 --> 00:17:19.640
Your student Roberta’s father.
- Sorry. Yes, Roberta.

205
00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:23.120
We cancelled the lesson,
but it wasn’t Roberta’s fault.

206
00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:26.240
It’s was because of me.
She is very good girl, really good.

207
00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:28.640
It was because of me...
I’m terribly sorry.

208
00:17:28.760 --> 00:17:32.080
It’s because of you?
- Yes, I had an accident.

209
00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:34.360
An accident?
- Well, I slipped.

210
00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:36.560
You slipped?
- Yes, I’m sorry.

211
00:17:36.680 --> 00:17:40.400
Hey, man. Tell me, how old you are?

212
00:17:40.520 --> 00:17:43.360
I’m 45, but slipping can happen
regardless of age.

213
00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:46.120
Roberta is 16 years old!

214
00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:49.360
Tell me, what you are teaching her
during these violin lessons?

215
00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:52.600
What do I teach? To play violin.
What’s going on? What is it?

216
00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:55.040
What it is?
- How should I know?

217
00:17:55.160 --> 00:18:00.760
What it is? Your photos, your names,
love notes! What is this?

218
00:18:00.880 --> 00:18:02.560
Good morning.
- Good morning.

219
00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:04.200
What is going on?
- My student’s…

220
00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:07.560
Your husband has an improper relation
with my daughter.

221
00:18:07.680 --> 00:18:10.160
What? No I don’t!
I had no idea.

222
00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:17.520
Declaration of love, photos,
some kind of escape plan to Salzburg.

223
00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:20.680
I told to Roberta about Salzburg
in classical music terms.

224
00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:24.440
It’s really awful and disturbing!
- What is going on?

225
00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:27.600
I have no idea what this means.
It’s absurd!

226
00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:31.440
I haven’t even proposed anything
to Roberta. - What?

227
00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:36.880
Roberta! Come here and explain.
- Roberta, go back in the car.

228
00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:40.880
It’s a lie! - Stop teasing the girl,
she is traumatized enough. Hell!

229
00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:42.240
It’s a lie!

230
00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:46.120
Please leave our house.
Please leave now.

231
00:18:46.240 --> 00:18:49.560
I wouldn’t go through the window.
- I will call the police.

232
00:18:49.680 --> 00:18:51.920
Police? I’ll call the police!

233
00:18:52.040 --> 00:18:54.600
Do you get it, man,
you are 45, Roberta 16!

234
00:18:54.720 --> 00:18:58.480
Do you know what to call it?
Paedophilia! You’re a paedophile!

235
00:18:58.600 --> 00:19:03.080
This is a very serious accusation!
You’ll be jailed for false accusation!

236
00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:07.200
Let the investigators investigate!
Paedophile!

237
00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:09.880
It’s an invasion! Get out!

238
00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:17.920
Roberta! Get out of the car!

239
00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:22.040
She will not come to this house again!

240
00:19:28.840 --> 00:19:32.040
This is... absolutely insane!

241
00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:43.920
What is going on? It’s insane.
This all, absolutely insane.

242
00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:48.600
Second time in a day
people show up at my door.

243
00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:53.200
Accusations fall… I’ll suffocate
under all these accusations.

244
00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:55.240
They wipe the floor with you!

245
00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:59.040
Come all, come and beat me!
Knock my teeth out!

246
00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:01.560
What’s now?
- I don’t know.

247
00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:06.640
The girl said it was her fantasy,
but father is insistent.

248
00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:09.680
Father wouldn’t allow her
to attend the lesson.

249
00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:13.920
At music school they dismissed me
until things are cleared.

250
00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:20.120
Out of nowhere this kind of stigma
stuck to you. It’s…

251
00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:27.320
What is happening? Why me?
Everything kind of sticks to me.

252
00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:30.280
Try to stay calm. Relax, relax.

253
00:20:30.400 --> 00:20:37.400
How can I stay calm!
I’m jobless, a stalker.

254
00:20:37.520 --> 00:20:43.520
Home will be taken away,
No job. Where I’m going to go?

255
00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:46.360
To the railway station’s tunnel
to squeak the violin?

256
00:20:46.480 --> 00:20:50.480
Not to the tunnel. You’ll come here!
You will live with us.

257
00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:52.760
You can move in tomorrow.

258
00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:56.280
Me and Mirjam, we’ll love you,
will take care of you.

259
00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:59.040
You’ll be like a son to me.
- Will you adopt me?

260
00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:27.320
Aksel, I believe you.

261
00:21:27.440 --> 00:21:32.080
I believe you’re innocent,
but you have to look for another job.

262
00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:38.120
I’ll manage. Most of world’s companies
will need a violin teacher. It’s easy!

263
00:21:38.240 --> 00:21:41.280
You have to take some classes,
to learn something real.

264
00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:44.120
I can help you.
- I thank you very much!

265
00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:50.320
I’ll lose my family, my home, my job
and now should throw away my vocation?

266
00:21:50.440 --> 00:21:54.560
I just want to help you.
I can see how this affects you.

267
00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:57.880
This suppressed anger,
it’s really dangerous.

268
00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:00.960
Then hire a bodyguard.
Let him stand on the door.

269
00:22:03.120 --> 00:22:05.560
We have lived in our burrows
for so long,

270
00:22:05.680 --> 00:22:08.320
who knows what kind of monsters
will crawl out.

271
00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:12.080
I was in the burrow,
you were hovering in the woods.

272
00:22:14.640 --> 00:22:20.160
I’ll admit. This has been a mistake.

273
00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:24.440
During our marriage
I have been seldom at home.

274
00:22:25.680 --> 00:22:29.320
At least I’ll try to be more at home
during the divorce.

275
00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:36.960
Ready for lights out?
- Lights out, bulb out and pack it in.

276
00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:53.640
Tiina Tiitus “Happy Relationship”

277
00:22:57.720 --> 00:23:01.280
Mirjam, darling.

278
00:23:04.520 --> 00:23:10.320
I was sitting here thinking.

279
00:23:12.040 --> 00:23:16.760
And thinking... And I worked it out.

280
00:23:18.200 --> 00:23:21.280
I thought about what you said.

281
00:23:22.680 --> 00:23:29.800
How to move our life to another level,
to the new and lovely level.

282
00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:34.280
No, I will not join Defence League.
- No, quite the opposite.

283
00:23:34.400 --> 00:23:39.720
You’ll become a pacifist?
- No, we’ll take…

284
00:23:39.840 --> 00:23:43.200
No, darling. We’re not taking the dog.
I have dog allergy.

285
00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:46.480
No, we are taking a baby.

286
00:23:48.120 --> 00:23:50.200
A real living baby.

287
00:23:50.320 --> 00:23:53.800
But you said that you don’t want...
Not your genes and so on.

288
00:23:53.920 --> 00:23:57.960
I thought it over and I’m ready now.

289
00:23:59.440 --> 00:24:02.240
Let there be a child.
- Really?

290
00:24:02.360 --> 00:24:07.240
Yes, if that’s the case.
I’ll do whatever it takes.

291
00:24:07.360 --> 00:24:12.680
Let’s take a child.
- Tauno. Thank you, darling!

292
00:24:12.800 --> 00:24:16.800
Let’s order a catalogue
and select a baby. That’s that.

293
00:24:19.200 --> 00:24:23.080
Yes, pretty much.
Thank you!

294
00:24:29.840 --> 00:24:32.600
Wow! What is going on?

295
00:24:32.720 --> 00:24:35.520
I decided to make a breakfast
for us all.

296
00:24:36.400 --> 00:24:39.720
Don’t you have to be at work?
- Oh, work can wait.

297
00:24:39.840 --> 00:24:44.960
So, let’s sit down and eat.
Mihkel, could you wake dad up.

298
00:24:45.080 --> 00:24:48.000
Dad is already up. He is in the middle
of an important phone call.

299
00:24:48.120 --> 00:24:49.280
Really?

300
00:24:49.400 --> 00:24:52.040
He is speaking with a guy
from symphony orchestra.

301
00:24:52.160 --> 00:24:54.080
They will make great music together.

302
00:24:54.200 --> 00:24:58.320
Exactly!
I will not betray my vocation.

303
00:24:58.440 --> 00:25:05.040
Well, that’s very nice.
Will you nerves be strong enough?

304
00:25:05.160 --> 00:25:08.480
I’m hardened.
- Normal!

305
00:25:08.600 --> 00:25:13.440
Mom, you should take jewellery up again
and not to churn out these stupid pies.

306
00:25:13.560 --> 00:25:15.200
You think so?

307
00:25:16.240 --> 00:25:19.920
You both can finally be
who you really want to be.

308
00:25:21.040 --> 00:25:24.440
Now when this marriage hypnosis
is finally over.

309
00:25:29.640 --> 00:25:31.160
Enjoy your meal!

310
00:25:32.480 --> 00:25:34.080
Bon appétit!

311
00:25:35.000 --> 00:25:37.560
Coffee?
- Yes, please.

312
00:25:37.680 --> 00:25:40.120
Egg? Right, you don’t eat eggs.

313
00:25:40.240 --> 00:25:43.960
Regular milk? Milk for anybody?

314
00:25:48.920 --> 00:25:51.480
Does somebody want milk?
- No, I don’t.

315
00:25:51.600 --> 00:25:54.040
For whom I cooked these eggs?

316
00:25:54.160 --> 00:25:59.440
Eggs? I already have.
- You don’t eat. Have you some.

317
00:25:59.560 --> 00:26:01.080
Thank you!

318
00:26:01.200 --> 00:26:04.360
These are free-ranged hens’ eggs.
- Yes, that’s very important.

319
00:26:04.480 --> 00:26:06.560
Why wouldn’t it be!
- Of course it is.

320
00:26:11.200 --> 00:26:15.000
I’m really glad you didn’t send all
to the devil because of this excess.

321
00:26:15.120 --> 00:26:19.120
Deal with these lunatics!
- I do understand your home situation.

322
00:26:19.240 --> 00:26:21.320
I’m really embarrassed.
I’m really sorry.

323
00:26:21.440 --> 00:26:23.440
I can’t understand,
what he was thinking.

324
00:26:23.560 --> 00:26:29.520
Are you cornered with this sale?
- No, no.

325
00:26:32.000 --> 00:26:34.320
Our deal is still on?

326
00:26:34.440 --> 00:26:38.160
All is well. Of course, Laura.
Yes, let’s continue.

327
00:26:38.280 --> 00:26:42.480
I got an idea. I’ll change the menu
in the whole restaurant chain.

328
00:26:42.600 --> 00:26:45.320
Maybe you can help me?
- Me?

329
00:26:45.440 --> 00:26:48.720
We don’t have to discuss
about this deal only.

330
00:26:50.680 --> 00:26:52.240
OK.

331
00:26:52.360 --> 00:26:58.840
I’ll come back and with big bang.
In a few days I’ll meet the orchestra.

332
00:26:58.960 --> 00:27:04.560
Hell, I will be the first violin.
I was born to be a virtuoso.

333
00:27:04.680 --> 00:27:09.880
Not to teach violin to half-witted.
To hell with teacher’s profession.

334
00:27:11.160 --> 00:27:14.920
I’ll get a flat and all big stages
in the world are waiting for me.

335
00:27:15.040 --> 00:27:17.800
You need no flat.

336
00:27:19.120 --> 00:27:22.720
You’ll come here.
Will keep an eye on Mirjam and...

337
00:27:22.840 --> 00:27:24.320
No, no. I...

338
00:27:24.440 --> 00:27:29.040
You’re the only man in this world
I can entrust Mirjam to.

339
00:27:29.160 --> 00:27:32.880
There’s no rush with moving.
Laura is very sensible.

340
00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:36.600
Be quiet. Listen to me.

341
00:27:41.400 --> 00:27:48.640
I told her I’ll agree with adaptation.
- Really? And Mirjam?

342
00:27:48.760 --> 00:27:51.760
Just one small thing was missing,
one small child.

343
00:27:51.880 --> 00:27:55.520
Now everything is 100% all right.
- Congratulations! You’ll be a father.

344
00:27:55.640 --> 00:27:58.560
Yes. Damn! I’ll be a father.

345
00:27:59.400 --> 00:28:01.960
Damn, I wouldn’t go
to the training assembly.

346
00:28:02.080 --> 00:28:08.240
I’d rather be at home.
Daddy is home! Bloody hell!

347
00:28:09.080 --> 00:28:11.240
Stand on your feet, man!

348
00:28:23.960 --> 00:28:29.160
Mona, over million clicks.
Really crazy, bloody hell!

349
00:29:03.360 --> 00:29:04.840
We have to talk, Aksel!

350
00:29:04.960 --> 00:29:08.840
I told you, Mirjam, we shouldn’t...
- I’m pregnant. You’ll be a father!

351
00:29:08.960 --> 00:29:10.600
What?
